EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ixagjvntbgyqemxxinqe.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable__A5fA6nyI8nrSqJWfaaJBQ_vqEZdRn6

# Where the web app is served, and so where a published tag's link points.
# Unset, the app falls back to the Vercel address built into src/lib/supabase.ts.
#
# This is inlined into the bundle at build time, not read at runtime, so a
# change needs a rebuild -- and on a phone that means a new app binary, since
# tagUrl() runs on the device, so phones keep minting links from whatever was
# compiled into their build until one ships.
#
# Setting it HERE was not enough on its own: an `expo export` with this value
# in the file, and again with it exported in the shell, produced a bundle that
# still carried the fallback -- the variable came out inlined as empty both
# times, and why was never run down. The deployed site gets its value from the
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL project variable in the Vercel dashboard instead. So
# treat this line as the intended value, not as proof the build uses it, and
# check a build before trusting it:
#
#   grep -ro plantparlour.org dist/ | wc -l    # 0 means it did not take
#
# The Vercel address stays the fallback in src/lib/supabase.ts and keeps
# answering forever: every tag link and QR code already printed points at it,
# and none of them can be rewritten.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://plantparlour.org
